# Assess the phase

When the user says "asses" or "assess", they mean: assess completion of the current phase and report. Do this without asking which phase they mean.

The current phase is the earliest week file in `docs/phases/week-NN.md` that is not fully complete against its "Done when" lines and the end-of-week line. If they name a week or phase, use that one instead.

Judge from the repo, the week file, and checks you can actually run. A ticked box is not enough when the "Done when" line is unmet, and an unticked box can still be met. Do not start the next phase unless they ask.

Mark every task with one of these:

- ✅ done: the "Done when" line is met
- 🟡 partial: some of it is met and some is not
- ⬜ open: not started, or skipped on purpose

Lead with whether the phase is complete, then a table whose first column is that marker.
